It doesn't look like you've done enough of the arithmatic when
making the comparison.

Twoweapon means much higher damage points by the time you
can use it.  And you only start doing twoweapon when you've
maxxed out your skills in both of the weapons you wield and that
only happens when you've maxxed out your luck.  So by the time
you twoweapon at all you never miss on any melee swing.

Add in the facts that AC has no practical lower bound with or
without a shield, and that reflection and MR can come from
mail and cloak.  As long as you're running a combat wombat who
doesn't cast spells regularly, you don't need a robe so you can
wear a [oMR.

Twoweapon advantages completely overwhelm shield advantages
in the phase of the game where twoweapon should be used,
around Medusa and below.



